===========================================
INSTRUCTIONS FOR REPORTING ABUSE
===========================================

1. UNDERSTAND THE SITUATION
   - This is an Anyone Protocol exit relay
   - Traffic appears to come from this IP but originates from users
   - We cannot identify individual users or their activities
   - We do not log user traffic or personal information

2. GATHER INFORMATION
   - Timestamp of the incident (UTC preferred)
   - Source IP address (if different from this relay)
   - Destination IP/domain and port
   - Type of activity (if known)
   - Any relevant logs or evidence

3. CONTACT INFORMATION
   - Primary Contact: {{ anon_relay_contact | default('abuse@example.com') }}
   - Abuse Contact: {{ anon_exit_notice_email | default('abuse@example.com') }}
   - Response Time: Within 24-48 hours

4. WHAT WE CAN DO
   - Investigate if the activity violates our exit policy
   - Block specific ports or protocols if needed
   - Provide technical information about our relay
   - Coordinate with law enforcement if legally required

5. WHAT WE CANNOT DO
   - Identify individual users
   - Provide user logs or personal information
   - Monitor or log user activities
   - Guarantee immediate resolution

===========================================
EXIT POLICY INFORMATION
===========================================

This relay blocks the following high-risk ports:
- Port 25 (SMTP)
- Port 587 (SMTP Submission)
- Port 465 (SMTPS)
- Port 2525 (SMTP Alternative)
- Port 3389 (RDP)
- Port 23 (Telnet)
- Port 3128 (HTTP Proxy)
- Port 5900 (VNC)
- Port 9999 (Custom high-risk)

All other traffic is allowed through this exit relay.

===========================================
